%% Source for Fig (sec:design-extensibility): the experiment-session lifecycle.
%% Render: bunx -y @mermaid-js/mermaid-cli -i session-lifecycle.mmd -o session-lifecycle.pdf
%% States mirror ExperimentSessionManager lifecycle, the readiness gate
%% (EnsureSetupIsReadyForStart / BuildSetupSnapshot) and the recovery statuses
%% (Recording / RecoveredIncomplete / Completed).
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Configuring
    Configuring --> Ready : readiness gate passes
    Ready --> Configuring : setup changed
    Ready --> Running : researcher starts the session
    Running --> Finished : researcher finishes
    Running --> Interrupted : disturbance (crash / disconnect)
    Interrupted --> Running : resume from last checkpoint
    Finished --> Configuring : reset for next participant
    Finished --> [*]

    note right of Configuring
        Setup prerequisites (D6):
        participant saved; eye tracker
        selected and licensed;
        calibration validated;
        reading material chosen.
        (Eye tracker and calibration are
        skipped for simulated sources, D5.)
    end note
    note right of Running
        The real-time adaptive loop runs;
        the session record is written
        incrementally (checkpointed).
    end note
    note left of Interrupted
        Recoverable (D3): the record is
        preserved up to the last checkpoint.
    end note
    note left of Finished
        Record sealed and exported
        (raw / processed, JSON / CSV).
    end note
